From 809cc36af2e4eae41e862560f1b01aa223f854ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:23:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linux-firmware: backport qcom Eliza QUPv3 firmware

linux-firmware 20261019 has no QUPv3 firmware for the Qualcomm Eliza
chipset. qcom/eliza/qupv3fw.elf was merged into linux-firmware.git after
the 20261019 release tag was cut. Without it the GENI serial engines the
ADSP shares with Linux (I2C on QUPv3 1 SE4 on the Eliza EVK) are never
loaded, and the ADSP crashes as soon as its protection domains start:

  qcom_q6v5_pas 3000000.remoteproc: fatal error received: qup_os_island.c:151:QUP_ERR_FATAL

Backport the upstream commit, update the WHENCE checksum, and package
the file as linux-firmware-qcom-eliza-qupv3fw like the other QUPv3
firmware.

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/firmware/linux-firmware.git/commit/?id=93b16ff1d54889fa1a40fa4ba8b7f308ce641c2a

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [meta-qcom specific]
---
 ...01-qcom-add-QUPv3-firmware-for-eliza.patch | 507 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../linux-firmware/linux-firmware_20261019.bb |   8 +-
 2 files changed, 513 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 meta/recipes-kernel/linux-firmware/linux-firmware/0001-qcom-add-QUPv3-firmware-for-eliza.patch

diff --git a/meta/recipes-kernel/linux-firmware/linux-firmware/0001-qcom-add-QUPv3-firmware-for-eliza.patch b/meta/recipes-kernel/linux-firmware/linux-firmware/0001-qcom-add-QUPv3-firmware-for-eliza.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..788648583d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/meta/recipes-kernel/linux-firmware/linux-firmware/0001-qcom-add-QUPv3-firmware-for-eliza.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,507 @@
